@raphaelmilliere @GaryMarcus @catherineols That is, if you start with a very very tiny model, you just get skip trigram heads (which don't involve any composition). 

As you make it larger, you get induction heads.

If you give the model more capacity still... you start to get into regimes we understand less well!

@raphaelmilliere @GaryMarcus @catherineols Just in case it's helpful, the following pseudo code is one way you might think about an induction head:

prev_token &lt;- attention(query=position-1, key=position, value=token)

induction_prediction &lt;- attention(query=token, key=prev_token, value=token)

